Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: only run the RRM link measurement handler for pending requests

OpenWrt's ubus binding lets userspace (usteer) send Link Measurement
Requests itself. hostapd_rrm_lm_req() builds those with dialog token 1 and
does not use the upstream hapd->link_mesr_req_active state, so every
response was passed to hostapd_handle_link_mesr_report(), which logs
"Unexpected Link measurement report, token 1" at MSG_INFO.

Only feed the upstream handler when it actually has a request pending. The
ubus notification is emitted separately, so usteer keeps working.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/25918
--- a/src/ap/rrm.c
+++ b/src/ap/rrm.c
@@ -409,7 +409,8 @@
 		hostapd_handle_nei_report_req(hapd, buf, len);
 		break;
 	case WLAN_RRM_LINK_MEASUREMENT_REPORT:
-		hostapd_handle_link_mesr_report(hapd, buf, len);
+		if (hapd->link_mesr_req_active)
+			hostapd_handle_link_mesr_report(hapd, buf, len);
 		hostapd_ubus_handle_link_measurement(hapd, buf, len);
 		break;
 	default:
